    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on stolen base upside, headlined by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (78.29), our highest-rated option. Facing Bradley, he offers a premium blend of leadoff-spot stability and a significant +14% boost from a favorable platoon matchup. Complementing him is **Yordan Alvarez** (72.69), who remains an elite foundational start; despite facing a lefty in Rogers, his exceptional xwOBA of 0.475 provides enough raw power to supersede platoon concerns. Both **Colt Keith** (69.64) and **Trea Turner** (69.07) provide secondary pillars of production, with the latter benefiting from a 5% wind-out advantage that should play well into the gaps against Manaea.\n\nStrategic roster optimization reveals a heavy reliance on favorable platoon dynamics. **Caleb Durbin** (54.29) earns a spot not just for his neutral platoon standing, but for the specific synergy of his matchup against the slow delivery of Seymour, which is a prime catalyst for his 100% stolen base potential. The closest call on the bench was **Casey Schmitt** (47.68). While he projected as a solid utility option, he ultimately fell short of the Zebras' 60+ threshold for an \"Elite\" start, as park factors and a lack of elite offensive velocity in his profile kept him behind the established starters like **Junior Caminero** (63.90).\n\nRisks for today center largely on the uncertainty surrounding the bottom of our order. **Dillon Dingler** is currently listed with a \"Lineup Pending\" tag; while his projected score of 51.57 is serviceable, any shift out of the #3 spot could dampen his utility. Additionally, we are monitoring the matchup between **Christian Yelich** and Meyer closely. While his score of 62.43 is strong, the threat of an elite hold pitcher potentially curbing his steal attempts\u2014an edge of -2%\u2014requires close observation once the game begins. Managers should also note that **Carson Benge** and **Jacob Gonzalez** were excluded from the lineup entirely, as both fell below our 40-point floor due to difficult matchups against Luzardo and Williams, respectively.",
